From 0f447dc0764ee6730b59c2c7158e7d1a05baf3c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Harris <adam@diaryx.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:37:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: surrounding text, replacement ranges and keyless
 insertText in the text input client
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

winit's NSTextInputClient answered nothing about the document:
`selectedRange` was always `{NSNotFound, 0}`, `attributedSubstringForProposedRange:`
always nil, and the `replacementRange` of `insertText:` and `setMarkedText:` was
ignored (two TODOs, "requires changing the event to report surrounding text" —
which winit-core has since done with `ImeRequestData::surrounding_text` and
`Ime::DeleteSurrounding`). And `insertText:` was reported only when it ended a
composition, on the assumption that any other text arrives as `KeyboardInput`.

Two macOS text features fell through:

- Press-and-hold accents: the input system reads the character before the
  caret, marks it, and replaces it with the chosen accent. With no text to read
  it never opened its menu, and the held key just repeated.
- The Emoji & Symbols picker, dictation and services insert with
  `insertText:` and no keystroke, so their text was dropped.

This change:

- keeps the surrounding text the application reports and answers
  `selectedRange` and `attributedSubstringForProposedRange:actualRange:` from it;
- resolves a `replacementRange` against it and reports `Ime::DeleteSurrounding`
  (relative to the caret) before the `Ime::Commit` in `insertText:`, or before
  the preedit in `setMarkedText:`;
- reports `insertText:` from outside `keyDown:` as `Ime::Commit`;
- does not forward a key repeat the input system swallowed (press-and-hold's
  menu is up), nor the key that then picks from the menu, as `KeyboardInput`.

An application that does not ask for the surrounding-text capability sees the
old behaviour, except that keyless insertions now arrive as `Ime::Commit` and a
swallowed repeat is no longer forwarded.
